owth and gastrointestinal hypertrophy</article-title><source>Nature Medicine</source><year>2002</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>289</fpage><lpage>293</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Nature Medicine||8|289||bib9|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pai</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Szabo</surname><given-names>IL</given-names></name><name><surname>Soreghan</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Atay</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kawanaka</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Tarnawski</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>PGE(2) stimulates VEGF expression in endothelial cells via ERK2/JNK1 signaling pathways</article-title><source>Biochem Biophys Res Commun</source><year>2001</year><volume>286</volume><fpage>923</fpage><lpage>928</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Biochem Biophys Res Commun||286|923||bib10|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11527387</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Qiao</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Stratagoules</surname><given-names>ED</given-names></name><name><surname>Martinez</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bile acid-induced activation of activator protein-1 requires both extracellular signal-regulated kinase and protein kinase C signaling</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>2000</year><volume>275</volume><fpage>15090</fpage><lpage>15098</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Biol Chem||275|15090||bib11|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10748108</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Richter</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jurek</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Wrba</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaserer</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Wurzer</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Karner Hanusch</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Marian</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cells obtained from colorectal microadenomas mirror early premalignant growth patterns <italic>in vitro</italic></article-title><source>Eur J Cancer</source><year>2002</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>1937</fpage><lpage>1945</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Eur J Cancer||38|1937||bib12|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12204677</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Richter</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Weiss</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Weinberger</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Furstenberger</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Marian</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Growth inhibition and induction of apoptosis in colorectal tumor cells by cyclooxygenase inhibitors</article-title><source>Carcinogenesis</source><year>2001</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>17</fpage><lpage>25</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Carcinogenesis||22|17||bib13|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11159736</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Seno</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Oshima</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ishikawa</surname><given-names>TO</given-names></name><name><surname>Oshima</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Takaku<